## READING THE TABLE
  wake     — died before the dispatch row existed. ZERO trace. Unrecoverable
             by design, and the reason the DISPATCHER must write the row,
             not the cell.
  dispatch — row is durable, work has not begun. An open lease: re-askable.
  execute  — same, plus wasted work. Still an open lease.
  commit   — THE QUESTION IN THE BRIEF. The commit exists in the worktree
             and never reached the remote. Reconcile records LOST, a
             NEGATIVE receipt. Without it this is indistinguishable from
             a clean run. (An earlier version recorded COMMIT here; the
             false repair is pinned in bug-false-repair.log and killed
             by I11b/I11c.)
  push     — the commit IS on the remote; only the outcome was lost.
             Reconcile repairs it from Dispatch-Id. Recoverable.
  outcome  — clean.
